    "text": "<p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/6b668b71-3579-49c2-86dd-354c73feaa3c-image.png\" style=\"width: 500px; height: 144px;\" /></p><p>Hex-<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math>-ene-<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>-ol on reaction with PCC forms&nbsp;Hex-<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math>-ene-<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>-one.</p><p>Hex-<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math>-ene-<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>-one on iodoform reaction gives pent-<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;enoic acid and iodoform.</p><p>Pent-<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;enoic acid on decarboxylation with soda lime forms but-<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>-ene.&nbsp;</p>",
